# Speech-to-Text (STT) Module Implementation Plan

## Goal Description
Build a modular, production-ready speech-to-text (STT) pipeline for the browser extension using `@xenova/transformers` (Transformers.js) and Whisper (`Xenova/whisper-small.en`). The architecture enforces strict separation of concerns across 4 decoupled modules so that the Whisper model can be swapped (e.g., from English-only to multilingual) solely by editing a single configuration file without modifying any other part of the pipeline.

---

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **In-Browser Execution & Storage**: `Xenova/whisper-small.en` is ~240MB quantized (ONNX). On the first run, Transformers.js automatically downloads the model files and caches them locally inside the browser's IndexedDB / Cache API. Subsequent runs load instantly from local cache with 0 network calls.
> - **Threading Architecture**: Transformers.js ASR inference can be compute-intensive. We provide both a direct module interface and an optional Web Worker bridge (`sttWorker.js`) so the sidepanel UI does not stutter during transcription.

